WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:21.875
had turned completely white and still.

2
00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.876
Gerald was so shocked, he could not speak.

3
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:27.898
His sister was now made of marble.

4
00:00:29.239 --> 00:00:30.760
At last he called down to Jimmy.

5
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.141
"Kathleen made the ring a wishing ring again.

6
00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.881
Then she wished she was a statue."

7
00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.362
"And is she?"

8
00:00:39.922 --> 00:00:40.522
asked Jimmy.

9
00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:43.063
"Come up and look."

10
00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.764
Jimmy climbed into the dinosaur.

11
00:00:45.784 --> 00:00:49.585
"She's really a statue," he said.

12
00:00:49.605 --> 00:00:51.885
"Let's go tell Mabel."

13
00:00:55.326 --> 00:00:57.087
Mabel was still hiding in the bushes.

14
00:00:58.087 --> 00:00:59.887
The boys told her about Kathleen.

15
00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:01.708
Mabel gasped.

16
00:01:03.348 --> 00:01:04.769
"What will happen next?"

17
00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:09.110
"She'll go back to normal," said Gerald.

18
00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.731
"But what about me?"

19
00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:13.011
said Mabel.

20
00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:17.353
"You don't know how frightening it is to be out here like this.

21
00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:19.093
Can't you get the ring?"

22
00:01:19.113 --> 00:01:24.295
"It may have turned to stone, but I'll try," said Gerald.

23
00:01:25.675 --> 00:01:27.756
Gerald climbed back into the dinosaur.

24
00:01:31.028 --> 00:01:32.790
The ring had not turned to marble.

25
00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:34.931
"I'm sorry, Kathleen."

26
00:01:35.472 --> 00:01:36.372
He took the ring.

27
00:01:39.115 --> 00:01:40.356
Then he gave it to Mabel.

28
00:01:40.376 --> 00:01:43.438
"Now you won't be afraid of anything."

29
00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:46.881
Mabel wanted to be closer to the dinosaur.

30
00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.045
Then she would be near Kathleen when her spell broke.

31
00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:58.310
After she crawled over to the dinosaur, she stood up and looked inside.

32
00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:02.477
"It'll be all right," she reassured Kathleen.

33
00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:04.197
"I'm nearby.

34
00:02:04.637 --> 00:02:06.958
Call me when you feel yourself getting better."

35
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.860
Inside her marble shell, Kathleen heard Mabel.

36
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.960
But she couldn't speak.

37
00:02:17.561 --> 00:02:21.343
The boys covered Mabel with the Ugly-Wuglies' clothes so she'd stay warm.

38
00:02:22.623 --> 00:02:25.164
They promised to return later to check on the girls.

39
00:02:30.388 --> 00:02:31.949
Then they went back to the school.

40
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.833
They told Mademoiselle that Kathleen was staying overnight with Mabel.

41
00:02:39.274 --> 00:02:41.175
The sun set and the moon rose.

42
00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:46.818
Mabel fell asleep.

43
00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:53.482
Inside the dinosaur Kathleen knew she must wait patiently for her own spell to break.

44
00:02:54.963 --> 00:02:56.264
Soon she fell asleep.

45
00:03:01.132 --> 00:03:03.833
Kathleen woke up suddenly in the middle of the night.

46
00:03:05.134 --> 00:03:06.654
The dinosaur was moving!

47
00:03:06.674 --> 00:03:09.796
"Oh, how dreadful!"

48
00:03:10.276 --> 00:03:10.756
she said.

49
00:03:10.776 --> 00:03:14.417
"The dinosaur must have come alive in the moonlight.

50
00:03:14.958 --> 00:03:17.719
That's what Gerald said happened to the statues."

51
00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:22.301
She was afraid to drop through the hole while the statue moved.

52
00:03:23.961 --> 00:03:24.902
But where was Mabel?

53
00:03:25.702 --> 00:03:27.483
What if the dinosaur stepped on her?

54
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:30.484
Kathleen peered through the hole.

55
00:03:31.316 --> 00:03:33.057
The dinosaur was moving faster.

56
00:03:34.378 --> 00:03:36.439
The floor of its stomach sloped downward.

57
00:03:37.539 --> 00:03:38.840
They were going downhill.

58
00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:43.543
Through the hole Kathleen saw grass and then stone.

59
00:03:45.304 --> 00:03:46.785
She heard the splash of water.

60
00:03:47.445 --> 00:03:48.385
They were near the lake.

61
00:03:49.706 --> 00:03:51.567
The dinosaur was about to go swimming!

62
00:03:52.548 --> 00:03:55.990
Kathleen jumped through the hole just as the dinosaur reached the lake.

63
00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.172
She raced into the Temple of Apollo.

64
00:04:06.828 --> 00:04:09.490
"Be still, little lady," said a voice.

65
00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:12.833
"I leap."

66
00:04:13.794 --> 00:04:17.477
Kathleen watched as the statue of Apollo leaped from the pedestal.

67
00:04:17.497 --> 00:04:22.041
"You're new here," said Apollo.

68
00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:26.404
"I'm quite new," said Kathleen.

69
00:04:26.424 --> 00:04:29.167
"I didn't know you could talk."

70
00:04:29.187 --> 00:04:31.629
"Why not?

71
00:04:32.009 --> 00:04:32.689
You can."

72
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.720
"But I'm alive," said Kathleen.

73
00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.062
"And so am I," said the statue.

74
00:04:41.082 --> 00:04:43.764
"I suppose so.

75
00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:47.145
But I thought I'd need the ring to see you."

76
00:04:47.165 --> 00:04:49.546
"That's for mortals.

77
00:04:50.006 --> 00:04:52.227
We statues can hear and see each other."

78
00:04:56.549 --> 00:04:58.970
At that, Apollo dove into the lake.

79
00:05:00.191 --> 00:05:02.552
Kathleen wanted to get Mabel and go home.

80
00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.021
She found Mabel sleeping under the pile of Ugly-Wugly clothing.

81
00:05:13.041 --> 00:05:14.921
"Wake up!"

82
00:05:15.422 --> 00:05:16.002
she called.

83
00:05:16.022 --> 00:05:20.483
"I want to go home," said Mabel.

84
00:05:20.503 --> 00:05:25.584
"So do I, but you can't go home like that.

85
00:05:26.065 --> 00:05:27.545
You're still too tall."

86
00:05:28.665 --> 00:05:29.946
Mabel closed her eyes.

87
00:05:29.966 --> 00:05:33.507
"Oh, Kathleen, I feel so funny.

88
00:05:33.527 --> 00:05:35.347
Am I shrinking?"

89
00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:38.548
"Yes!" said Kathleen.

90
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.421
"Now we can go home."

91
00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.742
"But what about you?"

92
00:05:42.762 --> 00:05:45.844
"What do you mean?

93
00:05:45.864 --> 00:05:48.326
I'm fine," said Kathleen.

94
00:05:48.346 --> 00:05:50.808
"Look at yourself."

95
00:05:51.848 --> 00:05:54.210
Kathleen looked down at her hands and her dress.

96
00:05:57.372 --> 00:05:59.394
"Why am I this horrid color?"

97
00:05:59.874 --> 00:06:00.515
she cried.

98
00:06:00.535 --> 00:06:03.737
"Don't you understand?"

99
00:06:04.237 --> 00:06:04.918
asked Mabel.

100
00:06:04.938 --> 00:06:07.920
"You're still a statue!"
